OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1787102284
OL,3,CBurnham says he is not embarrassed
OL,4,Cabout exchange with Trump aide
OL,5,Cimpersonator
OL,7,FWhen asked what step had been taken to
OL,8,Ffind out who had impersonated the
OL,9,FWhite House chief of staff, Burnham
OL,10,Freplied: "The correct action has been
OL,11,Ftaken here and in the US."
OL,13,FReports of the exchange of messages
OL,14,Ffirst emerged on Monday in the news
OL,15,Foutlet Politico.
OL,17,FThe British embassy in Washington was
OL,18,Fso concerned that it raised the matter
OL,19,Fwith the White House, according to two
OL,20,Fofficials who spoke to the media
OL,21,Forganisation.
OL,26,@rD@JOUsD@ZO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
