OL,3,CBurnham says he is not embarrassed
OL,4,Cabout exchange with Trump aide
OL,5,Cimpersonator
OL,7,FIn 1998, impressionist Jon Culshaw was
OL,8,Fput through the Downing Street
OL,9,Fswitchboard to then-premier Sir Tony
OL,10,FBlair while pretending to be then-
OL,11,Fleader of the Opposition Lord William
OL,12,FHague.
OL,14,FBlair realised instantly the call was
OL,15,Fa prank, but laughed and said: "It's
OL,16,Fquite a good imitation."
